@using UBookIt.Web.Rendering
@model IBookingFormView
@{
    var notice = Model.PrivacyNotice;
    var days = notice.RetentionDays;
}
@*
    What happens to the details this form is asking for. Rendered from ONE place because
    both flows collect contact details through _YourDetails, and a second copy is how the
    retention sentence would come to say two different things.

    THE FOUR STATEMENTS ARE FACTS ABOUT THIS PACKAGE, and every one of them is checkable
    against code in this repository: what is collected is what the fields above collect,
    why is what placement does with it, how long is `SiteBookingSettings.RetentionDays` —
    the same value the retention sweep acts on — and who can see it is the Sensitive data
    group check the backoffice applies. Nothing here asserts a lawful basis, a controller
    identity or a jurisdiction; those need a site's own judgement and live behind its own
    policy link.

    NO HEADING, deliberately. The document's heading outline is the site's, not the
    package's, and a heading inside a fieldset that already has a legend would be adding
    to an outline we do not own to solve a problem we do not have.

    NO CONTROL, deliberately. There is nothing to tick and nothing to agree to: the basis
    for holding a booker's details is performance of the booking, and an unrefusable
    tickbox would misrepresent that as consent — which would also imply a right to
    withdraw it and make the site's own records revocable.
*@
<div class="ubookit-privacy">
    <p>
        We use your name and email address — and your phone number, if you give one — to hold
        your booking, to identify it, and to confirm it with you.
    </p>
    <p>
        @if (notice.HasRetentionPeriod)
        {
            @* Stated from the configured period, never authored. A sentence written by hand
               here could claim a period the code does not keep, which is the failure this
               whole notice exists to prevent. *@
            <text>
                We keep them for @days @(days == 1 ? "day" : "days") after your booking. After that
                we remove them permanently — the booking itself is kept, without your details.
            </text>
        }
        else
        {
            @* The DEFAULT rendering, because retention is off unless a site turns it on. Saying
               nothing here would omit one of the four statements on most installs, invisibly.
               So it says what is true of this configuration and promises nothing. *@
            <text>
                We keep them until we remove them. This site has not set a period for removing
                them automatically.
            </text>
        }
        In this site's backoffice they can be seen only by staff who have been given access to
        personal data.
    </p>
    @if (notice.HasPolicyUrl)
    {
        <p>
            <a href="@notice.PolicyUrl">Read this site's privacy policy</a>
        </p>
    }
</div>
